{% extends "_page.html.j2" %}
{% from "_parts.html.j2" import contact_link %}
{% set providers = {'groq': 'Groq', 'gemini': 'Google Gemini', 'cloudflare_workers_ai': 'Cloudflare Workers AI', 'openrouter': 'OpenRouter', 'anthropic': 'Anthropic'} %}
{% set roles = {'extract': 'finds the facts in each report', 'synthesize': 'writes the summaries', 'verify': 'checks each claim against the facts'} %}
{% block title %}AI and editorial policy · {{ product }}{% endblock %}
{% block path %}/ai{% endblock %}
{% block description %}How {{ product }} uses AI to write its summaries, what is and isn't checked, and who is responsible.{% endblock %}
{% block heading %}AI and editorial policy{% endblock %}
{% block lede %}Our summaries are written by AI from the facts the sources report, and published without a separate check. Every AI-written story says so, right under its summary.{% endblock %}
{% block body %}
<section>
<h2 class="serif">What the AI does, and doesn't</h2>
<ul class="bullets">
<li>It writes a short summary, 60 to 120 words, and a few key facts from what the sources report, in plain words of its own.</li>
<li>It only sees facts we have taken from the reports, never the reports themselves, except for openly licensed ones.</li>
<li>It never sees reports from our "link only" sources.</li>
<li>It does not report, interview, give opinions or add facts of its own. If the sources don't say it, neither do we.</li>
</ul>
</section>
<section>
<h2 class="serif">The models we use</h2>
{% if model_rows %}
<ul class="bullets">
{% for m in model_rows %}
<li><b>{{ m.model.split('/')[-1] }}</b>, run by {{ providers.get(m.provider, m.provider) }}: {% for r in m.roles %}{{ roles.get(r, r) }}{{ ', ' if not loop.last }}{% endfor %}.{% if m.trains_on_inputs is false %} Under its terms, what we send is not used to train models.{% endif %}</li>
{% endfor %}
</ul>
{% endif %}
<p>Most are free services; when they run out, a paid model (Anthropic's Claude) takes over within a small daily budget. We only send them facts from news reports, never anything about you.</p>
</section>
<section>
<h2 class="serif">What is and isn't checked</h2>
<ul class="bullets">
<li><b>Not checked for accuracy:</b> no second model checks the summary's claims against the sources. AI can get details wrong, so follow the source links for anything important.</li>
<li><b>Not checked for wording:</b> the AI is told to write in its own words, but a summary may repeat phrases from a source.</li>
<li><b>No duplicates:</b> the same event is never published twice.</li>
</ul>
</section>
<section>
<h2 class="serif">Human review</h2>
<p>Stories are published automatically after passing our checks; no person reads them first. Stories on every subject get a summary, including crime, accidents, courts and deaths. An editor is responsible for everything on {{ product }}, and any story can be corrected or taken down at any time.</p>
</section>
<section>
<h2 class="serif">Found a mistake?</h2>
<p>Tell us at {{ contact_link() }}. We fix errors quickly and list every correction on our <a href="/corrections">corrections page</a>.</p>
</section>
{% endblock %}
